@startuml
title Employee & Task Management System — Domain Class Model
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
class User <<entity>> {
  - id: Long
  - fullName: String
  - email: String
  - password: String
  - role: Role
  - manager: User [0..1]
  - createdAt: LocalDateTime
  - active: boolean
}
class Task <<entity>> {
  - id: Long
  - title: String
  - description: String [0..1]
  - status: TaskStatus
  - priority: TaskPriority
  - deadline: LocalDate [0..1]
  - assignedTo: User [1]
  - assignedBy: User [1]
  - createdAt: LocalDateTime
  - updatedAt: LocalDateTime
}
enum Role {
  ADMIN
  MANAGER
  EMPLOYEE
}
enum TaskStatus {
  PENDING
  IN_PROGRESS
  DONE
}
enum TaskPriority {
  LOW
  MEDIUM
  HIGH
}
User "reports 0..*" --> "manager 0..1" User : manager
Task "0..*" --> "1" User : assignedTo
Task "0..*" --> "1" User : assignedBy {original}
User ..> Role : type
Task ..> TaskStatus : type
Task ..> TaskPriority : type
note bottom of User
password stores a BCrypt hash; APIs return DTOs, not entities.
EMPLOYEE requires an active MANAGER at assignment/creation time.
No reverse Java collection fields are implied by multiplicities.
end note
note bottom of Task
Relations are LAZY @ManyToOne without cascade deletion.
Original assignedBy is preserved; historical roles may change.
end note
@enduml
